    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass successfully. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed two failing tests in frai-core:\n\n### 1. **Governance test failure** (src/finetune/governance.test.js)\n**Issue**: `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was imported as a named export but only exported in the default export.\n**Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `/src/finetune/index.js` while maintaining the default export for backward compatibility.\n\n### 2. **Evaluation test failure** (src/eval/index.test.js)\n**Issue**: The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving references as its second parameter (bannedTerms), causing safe outputs like \"hello\" and \"friendly world\" to be incorrectly flagged as toxic.\n**Fix**: Removed the `bannedTerms` parameter from `toxicityMetric` and made it always use the default banned terms list, preventing confusion when called from `runEvaluations` which passes both outputs and references.\n\n**Result**: \u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files. All public exports remain intact.",
